WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.380
Your red blood cells are packed
with one oxygen-carrying protein.

2
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.530
Each molecule of it can carry
up to four oxygen molecules.

3
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.170
Blood leaves your lungs with that
protein 98 per cent saturated.

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:18.420
Then the same blood flows past resting
tissues and hard-working muscles alike.

5
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.690
So how does it know to give the
hardest-working muscles the most oxygen?

6
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.110
In this mission, you'll build the S-shaped
curve that shows how full the protein

7
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.260
is at each oxygen level.

8
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.810
Then you'll see what can
make that whole curve shift.

9
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.530
Your mission: explain how your blood
gives the hardest-working muscles the most

10
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.350
oxygen.
